msgstr "Mari just said she works a lot. Ask where with <0>kus</0>."

msgid "Mari just said she’s tired. Ask why with <0>miks</0>."
msgstr "Mari just said she’s tired. Ask why with <0>miks</0>."

msgid "Mari knows your name. <0>Kuidas läheb?</0> asks how you are."
msgstr "Mari knows your name. <0>Kuidas läheb?</0> asks how you are."

msgid "Mari starts a conversation. Pick each of your replies; a wrong one says why. Everything in it comes from lessons {first} to {last}, plus two phrases: <0/>, nice to meet you, and <1/>, goodbye."
msgstr "Mari starts a conversation. Pick each of your replies; a wrong one says why. Everything in it comes from lessons {first} to {last}, plus two phrases: <0/>, nice to meet you, and <1/>, goodbye."

msgid "Mari told you her name at the start."
msgstr "Mari told you her name at the start."

msgid "Meet someone in Estonian: say who you are, where you live and work, answer their questions and ask your own."
msgstr "Meet someone in Estonian: say who you are, where you live and work, answer their questions and ask your own."

msgid "name"
msgstr "name"

msgid "Nice to meet you"
msgstr "Nice to meet you"

msgid "not; no"
msgstr "not; no"

msgid "Now you ask. Pick the question that fits what Mari just said. Ask why with <0/>, and the answer starts with <1/>, because."
msgstr "Now you ask. Pick the question that fits what Mari just said. Ask why with <0/>, and the answer starts with <1/>, because."

msgid "Pärnu takes <0>-s</0>: <1>Pärnus</1>."
